secret scope `{{ secret_scope }}` (`git_token`) → OBO token.

## Architecture

```
src/{{ project_name }}/
├── agent.py        # plan -> draft -> validate -> open PR
├── config.py       # Settings (cloud={{ cloud }}, git_host={{ git_host }}, tf_dir={{ tf_dir }})
├── auth.py         # OBO / {{ headless_auth }} identity + git token
├── git_host.py     # {{ git_host }} branch + PR client (REST)
├── terraform.py    # fmt / validate / plan
├── llm.py          # model call that drafts/edits HCL
├── forms.py        # builds + auto-populates the change form
├── prompts/        # system / generate / review
└── tools/          # change_request, plan_reader -> ToolResult(success, data, error)
```

## The dynamic form

`forms/change_request.schema.json` declares the attributes a change can need
(resource type, name, environment, owner, etc.). `forms.build_form()`
**pre-fills** every field it can infer from the existing Terraform and repo
context, then marks the rest as `prompt: true`. The agent (or the CLI) only asks
the human for the unfilled fields. When you add a new managed resource type,
extend the schema — don't hard-code prompts in the agent.

