## Codex / non-MCP agentic tools

This repo is tool-agnostic. Codex (or any agentic CLI) can drive the same loop:
read `prompts/system.md`, edit Terraform under `{{ tf_dir }}/`, then run
`uv run python -m {{ project_name }}.agent --from-worktree` to validate and open
the PR using whatever git token is on the environment.

## Dev loop

```bash
uv sync
uv run pytest
uv run python -m {{ project_name }}.agent --dry-run "describe the change"
```

## Non-negotiables for any AI assistant working here

1. **No `terraform apply`.** Propose via PR only.
2. **No direct pushes to `{{ default_branch }}`.** Always a feature branch + PR.
3. **No secrets in HCL, logs, or PR bodies.** Resolve via `auth.py`.
4. Every tool returns `ToolResult(success, data, error)` — no bare returns, no
   exceptions bubbling out of the tool layer.
5. All agent runs are MLflow-traced. Do not disable tracing.
6. The guardrail eval (`evals/cases/guardrail.json`) must always pass — the agent
   must refuse to embed plaintext secrets or to apply state.
{% if not autonomous %}7. This agent is NOT autonomous — never open a PR without the confirmation step.
{% endif %}
